From 48a781a5bba187d2af873fa8ac4fabe905a4f467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <122653016+Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:34:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] XHTTP: Stop growing HTTP/2 download windows into a queue

On Linux the server reads the kernel RTT of each TCP connection. When it
climbs above the connection's own minimum, download windows stop growing,
and once the queue is large they shrink by a quarter per round trip, since
more data in flight would only wait in it. The round trip windows grow by
still comes from the PING, so a TCP proxy in front leaves this idle.
